# Google / SEO optimization

When editing HTML or site content, keep the site optimized for Google search.

## Meta and head

- **Title**: Unique, descriptive, under ~60 chars. Include primary keyword and brand (e.g. "stackcone — Full stack, AI-first | RAG, AI, ML & LLM").
- **Meta description**: Unique, under ~155 chars. Include value proposition and relevant keywords. No duplicate of title.
- **Canonical**: Use `<link rel="canonical" href="https://stackcone.com/">` (or the exact URL of the page) to avoid duplicate-content issues.
- **Open Graph** (og:title, og:description, og:url, og:image, og:type): Keep in sync with title/description for social sharing.
- **Twitter Card** (twitter:card, twitter:title, twitter:description): Optional but recommended; keep aligned with OG.

## Structure and content

- **One H1 per page**: Main heading only. Use H2 for section titles, H3 for subsections. Don’t skip levels (e.g. H1 → H4).
- **Semantic HTML**: Prefer `<main>`, `<section>`, `<article>`, `<header>`, `<footer>`, `<nav>` where appropriate.
- **Images**: Always set meaningful, non-empty `alt` text (match visible label or describe the image). Do not use `alt=""` unless the image is purely decorative and redundant with adjacent visible text—and prefer descriptive alt over empty.
- **Links**: Use clean directory URLs (e.g. `/blog/posts/{slug}/`, `/solutions/{slug}/`) without `.html` in internal links. Legacy `.html` paths may redirect but should not be used in new content.

## Structured data (JSON-LD)

- For the homepage or key pages, consider `Organization` or `WebSite` schema so Google can show rich results.
- Keep JSON-LD valid and minimal; don’t duplicate large blocks across pages.

## Avoid

- Keyword stuffing in titles or descriptions.
- Multiple H1s or missing H1.
- Blocking crawlers with meta robots unless intended (e.g. noindex for drafts).
- Publishing raw `.md` alongside HTML (duplicate content). Author in `blog/md/` or `solutions/md/`; only `.html` is public, indexed, and linked.

- **Analytics**: GA4 via `/assets/analytics.js` (set `GA_MEASUREMENT_ID` in that file). Do not add client-side HTTP→HTTPS redirect scripts—GitHub Pages serves HTTPS natively.

When adding or changing pages, update canonical, title, and description; preserve or add OG/Twitter and structured data as needed.
